# The report templates are embedded with `include_str!` and the golden documents
# are compared byte-for-byte, so git must not rewrite their line endings. With a
# CRLF checkout on Windows the template-sourced newlines become CRLF while the
# advisory text coming from Rust string literals stays LF, and `html_golden`
# fails on that difference alone.
*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
